  "id": "hypercolumn",
  "term": "hypercolumn",
  "definition": "In this source, a hypercolumn refers to a multi-scale combination of image features used to capture more complete information about a target, such as lesions with different sizes and shapes. It is described as part of a feature-fusion approach for image segmentation, but the packet does not provide a fuller general definition beyond that use.",
